# The container nodes

`LoomAst` defines the container nodes — the tree the parse pipeline builds from a file's wefts. A `LoomDocument` holds one `LoomSection` per heading or divider, and each section holds a `LoomHeading` plus its body wefts. The tree is flat: heading level is for the reader, never nesting, and a division stands between the sections around it rather than holding them.

## The heading

A `LoomHeading` is what opens a section. It carries the parts the `HeadingWeft` carried: a `marker`, an optional title, an optional language `specifier`, and an optional `sink`. The marker is a heading's run of `#` marks, or a divider's dashes when a divider opens the section. A division's title is its label, the line of prose directly above the divider, so the heading of a division spans both lines. A bare divider gives a heading with no title. A divider carries no specifier and no sink.

=>

export const LoomHeadingSchema = loomNode('LoomHeading', {
  marker: Schema.Union([HeadingStartTokenSchema, DividerTokenSchema]),
  title: Schema.optional(HeadingTitleTokenSchema),
  specifier: Schema.optional(SpecifierTokenSchema),
  sink: Schema.optional(SinkTokenSchema),
})
export type LoomHeading = typeof LoomHeadingSchema.Type

## The section

A `LoomSection` is one structural unit, opened by a heading at any level or by a divider. Its body is two ordered runs of wefts: the `preamble` before the first transition, and the `code` after — the `=>` and `~` chunks in source order. A `{TOC}` section carries a third run, its `entries` — the toc wefts that list the book's parts and chapters. An ordinary section has none.

=>

export const LoomSectionSchema = loomNode('LoomSection', {
  heading: LoomHeadingSchema,
  preamble: Schema.Array(PreambleWeftSchema),
  code: Schema.Array(SectionBodyWeftSchema),
  entries: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(TocWeftSchema)),
})
export type LoomSection = typeof LoomSectionSchema.Type

## The frontmatter

A `LoomFrontmatter` is a chapter's opening block, parsed. It carries the membership line's `part`, `partName`, `chapter` or `discussion`, and `title`, the `trope` the loom belongs to, and the block's fields: the `package` a `{Tangle}` section writes to, the `language` its sections inherit, and the `status` and `priority` a roadmap reads. A numbered part fills `part`; a numberless one fills `partName` alone. Every slot is optional, so a partial block still parses to a node the diagnostics can fault, and a file with no block has no frontmatter at all. A loom whose block names a `discussion` is a discussion rather than a chapter, as the chapter "Discussions" describes. A loom whose block names a `trope` is a chapter of that trope, as Part XIII, Tropes, describes.

=>

export const LoomFrontmatterSchema = loomNode('LoomFrontmatter', {
  part: Schema.optional(FrontmatterPartTokenSchema),
  partName: Schema.optional(FrontmatterPartNameTokenSchema),
  chapter: Schema.optional(FrontmatterChapterTokenSchema),
  discussion: Schema.optional(FrontmatterDiscussionTokenSchema),
  trope: Schema.optional(FrontmatterTropeTokenSchema),
  title: Schema.optional(FrontmatterTitleTokenSchema),
  package: Schema.optional(FrontmatterValueTokenSchema),
  language: Schema.optional(FrontmatterValueTokenSchema),
  status: Schema.optional(FrontmatterValueTokenSchema),
  priority: Schema.optional(FrontmatterValueTokenSchema),
})
export type LoomFrontmatter = typeof LoomFrontmatterSchema.Type

## The document

A `LoomDocument` is the root, the implicit module named by its file. Its `frontmatter` is the opening block, when the file has one; its `preamble` is the run of wefts between that block and the first heading — carrying any value Warps; and its `sections` are the flat list that follows. Every slot may be empty.

=>

export const LoomDocumentSchema = loomNode('LoomDocument', {
  frontmatter: Schema.optional(LoomFrontmatterSchema),
  preamble: Schema.Array(PreambleWeftSchema),
  sections: Schema.Array(LoomSectionSchema),
})
export type LoomDocument = typeof LoomDocumentSchema.Type

## What this module draws on

Each container is a `loomNode` built from Effect's `Schema`. The heading's subtokens come from `LoomTokens`; the preamble and body weft types come from `Weft`.

=>

import { Schema } from 'effect'
import { loomNode } from '#ast/LoomNode'
import {
  DividerTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterChapterTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterDiscussionTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterTropeTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterPartTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterPartNameTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterTitleTokenSchema,
  FrontmatterValueTokenSchema,
  HeadingStartTokenSchema,
  HeadingTitleTokenSchema,
  SinkTokenSchema,
  SpecifierTokenSchema,
} from './LoomTokens'
import { PreambleWeftSchema, SectionBodyWeftSchema, TocWeftSchema } from './Weft'

